    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9688" root="حى: or حى and حيو" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْيَى</span></b>  in the saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْيَى مِنْ ضَبٍّ</span> [<i>More longlived than a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضبّ</span>, a kind of lizard, which is supposed to live seven hundred years,] is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَيَاةُ</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  In the sayings <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْيَى مِنْ هَدِىٍّ</span> [<i>More
shy,</i> or <i>bashful, than the bride</i>] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْيَى مِنْ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَدَّرَةٍ</span> [<i>More shy,</i> or <i>bashful, than a girl kept
behind the curtain</i>] it is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَيَآءُ</span>. (TA.)

